NF and\n  proven intractable on structured DNNF, d-DNNF and FBDD unless P=NP\n  (arxiv 2601.03523). SDD is what makes the variance half of this\n  mission possible at all.\n- Compilation cost, memory, and repeated-query latency measured on\n  actual candidate families before any production claim.\n\n### Activation triggers (per the parked-appendix ruling)\n\nNamed trigger, not drift: (a) a live decision hits\n`:observation-universe-out-of-bounds` — the typed refusal\n`observation_model.clj` raises when a declared universe exceeds\n`max-tokens` (10) — e.g. via hole-retention feeding declarations at\nscale; or (b) a demonstrated case where rate uncertainty at current\nsample sizes flips a ranking. Both are events the record already\ncarries, rather than a judgement about when enumeration stops being\ncomfortable. Whoever hits either names it as the trigger and this\nmission leaves IDENTIFY; nobody widens quietly.\n\n### Scope out\n\nEverything the plain A design covers today; the calibration collection\nitself (point 5, its own thread); any change to checkable-channel\nexactness (proven immune to coupling — that theorem is a boundary, not\na limitation).\n\n### Relationship to plop-2026\n\nSuccessor: it exists so the paper's A can be honest about its scale and\nuncertainty limits and point HERE, rather than gesturing at compilers\nmid-design. Nothing in it blocks or is blocked by the current A work.\n\nPlop-2026 completion is the expected ordering, not the activation\ncondition — the triggers above govern, and one could fire first.\nTrigger (a)'s premise, hole retention feeding declarations, landed on\n2026-09-20 in futon2 3b5557aa.\n\n### tl;dr\n\n- [ ] The A query interface has a WMC backend using cached SDD compilations of the declared common-cause model.\n- [ ] WMC marginal and joint queries match exact enumeration, including the matched-marginal total-G invariance control under point beliefs and product preferences.\n- [ ] Compiled query means and variances match small-model calculations while preserving shared rate-parameter identity.\n- [ ] Compiled joint queries compute the state-observation mutual information needed for total G under spread beliefs.\n- [ ] Compilation cost, memory use, and repeated-query latency are measured on actual candidate families."}], :pinned-at "2026-09-21T03:41:48.035185967Z", :tension-rule :lifecycle-sections}, :pattern-source {:id "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness.flexiarg#3422be8e2d242d488b20f10879367542a2c0e23311b0e2dee9d976548876cdfe", :path "/home/joe/code/futon3/library/buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness.flexiarg", :file "078454d61dbdb63116ca03fcefae5a3c26bce0970c8da5fc071cda5d0ceb9728-3422be8e2d242d488b20f10879367542a2c0e23311b0e2dee9d976548876cdfe.source", :sha256 "3422be8e2d242d488b20f10879367542a2c0e23311b0e2dee9d976548876cdfe", :revision "7fc6a05004aa3e601e53eba633d62213da0af4b2"}, :retrieval [{:retriever "embedding", :rank 34, :retriever-rank 34, :raw {:pattern_id "buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness", :embedding_rank 34, :relevance 0.3829070558195216, :posterior_mean 0.5, :posterior_n 0, :label "self-graded", :posterior_rank 34}}]}, :proposal-id "a787731aeb0c5daedf2d2983addb4f268dc943168a50104e29369f2ffd08862a"} {:schema :wm/cascade-proposal-v1, :status :proposed, :origin :retrieval-proposed, :target "M-a-wmc-scaling", :pattern "campaign-coherence/shared-standard-has-no-single-owner", :evidence {:target {:id "M-a-wmc-scaling", :kind :mission, :source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/M-a-wmc-scaling.md#40a494e8d9f24c344cc473637f8f0a2ca64feaf4f836092f834493d3044a0220", :citations [{:source "/home/joe/code/futon2/holes/M-a-wmc-scaling.md#40a494e8d9f24c344cc473637f8f0a2ca64feaf4f836092f834493d3044a0220", :lines [23 150], :quote "\n### Why this exists: three limitations of the A now being built\n\nThe current A (design-of-record 67152883) is deliberately minimal:\njudgement tokens in declarations, channel rates from counted-denominator\nrecord searches, one bina