ent.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment s1 with relation 'context': the title is the file's identity, the entry point to reading what exists.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Read the mission's existing material — status, sessions, phase discipline — and record where it stands before authoring anything."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A cascade is to be constructed for a problem.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Fragment s1 (offsets 2-29): the header names the existing file M-futonzero-prelim-practice, the first thing read, not produced.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A mission document exists and is being read before anything is constructed for it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Reading takes time, and a plausible cascade can be written from the problem statement in minutes.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Sentence s2-s3 (offsets 30-195): the file records two operator sessions (2026-08-15 shape, 2026-09-28 appended below) that a summary-only reading would skip.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "A plausible reading of the mission could be written from the mission statement alone without reading its appended operator sessions."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Read the four sources first and record where they disagree.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first.flexiarg", :sha256 "04b442f40edd33be35382de2355944a0135c50dbefce4a7ec5967378ec21d81e"}, :situation-source "Sentence s2 (offsets 30-116): 'OPEN — HEAD — operator shape captured 2026-08-15' records where the mission actually is.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The mission's own state (OPEN, HEAD, not yet IDENTIFY) decides what work fits; work authored without reading it restates the mission statement."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [0], :pattern "cascade-construction/read-what-exists-first"} {:pattern-rationale "The banner fixes where the mission stands and refuses to over-advance it.", :fragment-span {:start 43, :end 54}, :occurrence-id ["apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule" 1], :roles ["context" "condition"], :source-sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f", :sentence-id "s2", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule", :objects {:G {:text "    Analysis capacity exists — the register's standard and the causal through-line were both produced by the same agents who spent weeks patching — but it activates only when the system is stopped; unscheduled, that happens exactly when the operator's patience breaks, which is the most expensive possible trigger.\n\n    + evidence: APM: 08-27 register standard unused for twelve days; 09-08 end-to-end analysis within hours of the forced halt. Convergent wm mechanism: self-halting loop that bells its owner; ruled walkthroughs as scheduled halts; steward drain contract.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Fragment s2 (offsets 43-54): 'OPEN — HEAD' fixes the stage explicitly in the banner.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Pin the stopping/advance condition on the mission's declared lifecycle stage so advancing needs no one's judgment call."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Fixes keep landing but the same defect families keep recurring.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s2 (offsets 30-116): status stays 'OPEN — HEAD' while a second operator session is recorded.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission keeps accumulating operator sessions without advancing its lifecycle state."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Against a live campaign, every fix is minimal by necessity — nobody is ever authorized or situated to stop and rebuild a seam, because stopping always costs something visible today while the seam's cost is spread across future incidents.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s3 (offsets 117-195): the second session is 'appended below' rather than the file being restructured.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Against a live workspace, the mission cannot stop and rebuild itself; each session appends minimally."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Put the halt on the schedule so it needs no one's courage: between waves, stop cleanly, re-read the register, and convert \"guarantee: none\" rows into mechanisms — the register defines done as \"recurrence requires a named mechanism to fail\". Only then start the next wave. Register stewards drain between waves so no raw queue reaches the operator.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s4 (offsets 196-243): 'Not yet IDENTIFY' — the mission refuses to advance before its condition is met.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Analysis capacity exists in the recorded sessions but activates only when the lifecycle stage is respected; advancing unscheduled is the most expensive trigger."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [1], :pattern "apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule"} {:pattern-rationale "The status is dated evidence of what the operator said, not an interpretation of it.", :fragment-span {:start 57, :end 116}, :occurrence-id ["agent/evidence-over-assertion" 2], :roles ["context"], :source-sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248", :sentence-id "s2", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion", :objects {:G {:text "    Evidence transforms agent output from \"trust me\" to \"check this.\" It enables verification, correction, and cumulative trust-building.\n\n    + evidence: Fulab PUR/PSR templates require anchors/certificates (`src/futon3/fulab/pattern_competence.clj`), and claim verification is enforced via `fulab-pattern-claim` + `fulab-pattern-check`.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Fragment s2 (offsets 57-116): 'operator shape captured 2026-08-15; second operator session' plus the dated '2026-09-28' in s3.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Anchor each status element to a dated, identifiable operator session."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The agent's outputs need to be verifiable by other agents, humans, or future selves.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Fragment s2 (offsets 57-116): the status is stated as dated facts about operator sessions.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission's status claims need to be checkable by future readers of the file."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Assertions without anchors are indistinguishable from confabulation. Observers cannot tell if the agent is reporting reality or generating plausible-sounding noise.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Sentence s2 (offsets 57-85): the claim carries the explicit date '2026-08-15' as its anchor.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "An undated or unanchored status line would be indistinguishable from an invented one."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Require every substantive claim to point to evidence: a file path, a trace event, a test result, a quotation. If evidence is unavailable, emit the claim as provisional with an expiry and a verification path. Make \"unsupported claim\" a detectable violation, not just a style preference.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/agent/evidence-over-assertion.flexiarg", :sha256 "28425a05c4a87cbfe3147c1998e83701b8519b42c1796f1d0f25b4b039271248"}, :situation-source "Sentence s3 (offsets 117-195): '(appended below, ...)' points to the verbatim record backing the claim.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Dated anchors turn the banner from 'trust me' into 'check this' — the sessions are appended in the file for verification."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [2], :pattern "agent/evidence-over-assertion"} {:pattern-rationale "The operator bounds how the sketch may be acted on; conduct is not assumed from intent.", :fragment-span {:start 201, :end 224}, :occurrence-id ["problems/process-conduct-is-unassured" 4], :roles ["condition" "contrast"], :source-sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2", :sentence-id "s4", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/process-conduct-is-unassured", :objects {:G {:text "    The record's own caveat applies to this node too: until a checker refuses process work that lacks these assurances, this node is prose — but prose with a committed source pointer.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, section 0 (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05) and section 1 S1 problem/now fields.", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Fragment s4 with relations 'condition','contrast': the constraint defines the boundary later work must land on.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Treat the design-not-build boundary as the landing point for whatever will assure it; the mission states the requirement, not the mechanism."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The WM, in operation, commissions work, receives returns, closes records, and surfaces results.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Sentence s3 (offsets 141-195): 'a design sketch the operator asked to develop'.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The operator commissions work on this mission (develop a design sketch)."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, per the record: the WM in operation is an orchestrator whose assurance stack (run-era ledger, catalogued checks, conformance certificates, stepper) covers the CONTROL LOOP's decisions; nothing yet assures its PROCESS conduct — and the eight-trap catalogue (N-process-trap-recording-conventions section 1) was harvested from precisely this class of activity, performed by this campaign's own agents with far more context than the machine will have. Handoff machinery exists un-assured (bells, parks, packets are prose conventions, not typed objects any checker refuses on); the tick's closure boundary excludes the seven store-owning namespaces of the full-loop click path; and T7/T8 have no WM instances today and no checker that would refuse one. (source: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, S1, Joe's commissioning question of 2026-09-05 quoted in section 0)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Fragment s4 (offsets 201-224): the constraint is stated as inline emphasis '*as design*, not build)', a convention rather than a typed gate.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The commissioning is prose; nothing yet checks that the commissioned conduct (design, not build) is actually followed."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer process-conduct assurance; solving the problem is scoped by the record's solved-field, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Sentence s4 (offsets 196-243): the constraint is recorded verbatim in the operator's own words at the point of commissioning.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Until a checker refuses build-shaped work on this sketch, the constraint is prose — but prose with a committed source in the mission file."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [4], :pattern "problems/process-conduct-is-unassured"} {:pattern-rationale "Refuses to claim the next phase before its stopping condition is met.", :fragment-span {:start 226, :end 242}, :occurrence-id ["apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule" 5], :roles ["condition"], :source-sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f", :sentence-id "s4", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule", :objects {:G {:text "    Analysis capacity exists — the register's standard and the causal through-line were both produced by the same agents who spent weeks patching — but it activates only when the system is stopped; unscheduled, that happens exactly when the operator's patience breaks, which is the most expensive possible trigger.\n\n    + evidence: APM: 08-27 register standard unused for twelve days; 09-08 end-to-end analysis within hours of the forced halt. Convergent wm mechanism: self-halting loop that bells its owner; ruled walkthroughs as scheduled halts; steward drain contract.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Fragment s4 (offsets 226-242): 'Not yet IDENTIFY' defers the advance to the lifecycle's own condition.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Let the lifecycle schedule, not courage, decide when IDENTIFY begins."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Fixes keep landing but the same defect families keep recurring.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s2 (offsets 30-116): 'OPEN — HEAD' persists after both recorded sessions.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission has received input (two sessions) but its lifecycle state has not moved."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Against a live campaign, every fix is minimal by necessity — nobody is ever authorized or situated to stop and rebuild a seam, because stopping always costs something visible today while the seam's cost is spread across future incidents.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s4 (offsets 226-242): the phase advance is explicitly withheld, 'Not yet IDENTIFY'.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The mission cannot simply declare itself into the next phase; that costs judgment nobody is situated to spend."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Put the halt on the schedule so it needs no one's courage: between waves, stop cleanly, re-read the register, and convert \"guarantee: none\" rows into mechanisms — the register defines done as \"recurrence requires a named mechanism to fail\". Only then start the next wave. Register stewards drain between waves so no raw queue reaches the operator.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentences s2-s3 (offsets 57-195): the captured operator shape and appended session are the standing material waiting for the scheduled advance.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Analysis capacity (the captured shape, the appended sketch request) already exists in the file; it activates when the lifecycle advances on schedule, not when patience breaks."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [5], :pattern "apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule"} {:pattern-rationale "Discipline is anchored to a named scheduled entrypoint rather than ad-hoc judgment.", :fragment-span {:start 270, :end 305}, :occurrence-id ["problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint" 6], :roles ["dependency" "rationale"], :source-sha256 "2ff7e4e388e7dc0c8f335dc4f89f56ae577124017c425f5a44b9c18b6f48f2bd", :sentence-id "s5", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint", :objects {:G {:text "    The census (library-loop L1) found only six problem-stating nodes for 1256 patterns, so most @why edges had nothing to land on; minting the dossier problems as nodes is the recorded-corpus repair.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-assurance-band-batch6.md, section \"## R10 — Scheduled entrypoint\", subsection \"The problem it solves\".", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint.flexiarg", :sha256 "2ff7e4e388e7dc0c8f335dc4f89f56ae577124017c425f5a44b9c18b6f48f2bd"}, :situation-source "Fragment s5 with relations 'dependency','rationale': the discipline is delegated, not invented here.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Treat the named lifecycle document as the landing point for why phase discipline is delegated to it."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A pattern's rationale is that it answers the problem this node states.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint.flexiarg", :sha256 "2ff7e4e388e7dc0c8f335dc4f89f56ae577124017c425f5a44b9c18b6f48f2bd"}, :situation-source "Sentence s5 (offsets 244-325): 'per `futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle.md`, HEAD preserves the'.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission's phase discipline needs a rationale anchored to an entrypoint."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, verbatim from the dossier: R10 solves unattended liveness: the roster places **“Scheduled entrypoint”** in PERCEIVE's assurance band (`control-stages.edn:39`; control-stage numbering). Contract R10 requires recurring execution without operator intervention plus a queryable trace (`docs/futon-aif-completeness.md:260-268`; contract R10). Catalogue R10 sharpens liveness to observable state change, not a scheduler firing or painting green no-op rows (`p4ng/sec-catalog.tex:156-158`; catalogue R10). The equation registry gives R10 no equation and classifies it as plumbing (`aif-equations.edn:472-473`; control-stage R10). R10 therefore solves repeatable entry into perception while refusing to confuse wakeups with useful work. (source: futon2 holes labs wm-contract PROBLEMS-assurance-band-batch6.md, R10, The problem it solves)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint.flexiarg", :sha256 "2ff7e4e388e7dc0c8f335dc4f89f56ae577124017c425f5a44b9c18b6f48f2bd"}, :situation-source "Fragment s5 (offsets 270-305): the backticked path names the authority explicitly rather than leaving the rule implicit.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "Ad-hoc judgment about what HEAD means would be unverifiable; the lifecycle document states the recurring rule."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer it; solving the problem itself is scoped by the dossier's residual-problems list, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint.flexiarg", :sha256 "2ff7e4e388e7dc0c8f335dc4f89f56ae577124017c425f5a44b9c18b6f48f2bd"}, :situation-source "Sentence s5-s7 (offsets 244-428): the document's rule (preserve voice, no design, no curriculum) is then applied concretely.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Minting the dependency on a named document is the recorded-corpus repair: without it, the phase rule had nothing authoritative to land on."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [6], :pattern "problems/r10-scheduled-entrypoint"} {:pattern-rationale "The file asserts its own conduct boundary explicitly rather than leaving it inferred.", :fragment-span {:start 373, :end 389}, :occurrence-id ["problems/process-conduct-is-unassured" 8], :roles ["condition" "contrast"], :source-sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2", :sentence-id "s6", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "problems/process-conduct-is-unassured", :objects {:G {:text "    The record's own caveat applies to this node too: until a checker refuses process work that lacks these assurances, this node is prose — but prose with a committed source pointer.\n    + evidence: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, section 0 (Joe, verbatim, 2026-09-05) and section 1 S1 problem/now fields.", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Fragment s6 with relations 'condition','contrast': the boundary is asserted explicitly rather than left inferred.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Treat the not-design boundary as the landing point for whatever assures it; the mission states the rule, not its enforcement."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    The WM, in operation, commissions work, receives returns, closes records, and surfaces results.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Fragment s6 (offsets 373-389): 'It is not design'.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission file itself declares conduct rules (HEAD is not design)."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    The problem, per the record: the WM in operation is an orchestrator whose assurance stack (run-era ledger, catalogued checks, conformance certificates, stepper) covers the CONTROL LOOP's decisions; nothing yet assures its PROCESS conduct — and the eight-trap catalogue (N-process-trap-recording-conventions section 1) was harvested from precisely this class of activity, performed by this campaign's own agents with far more context than the machine will have. Handoff machinery exists un-assured (bells, parks, packets are prose conventions, not typed objects any checker refuses on); the tick's closure boundary excludes the seven store-owning namespaces of the full-loop click path; and T7/T8 have no WM instances today and no checker that would refuse one. (source: futon2 holes problems P-assured-process.md, S1, Joe's commissioning question of 2026-09-05 quoted in section 0)\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Sentence s6 (offsets 326-404): the rule is stated inline in the operator's banner voice, not as a typed gate.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The declaration is prose in a mission file; no checker refuses design-shaped content in HEAD."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer process-conduct assurance; solving the problem is scoped by the record's solved-field, not by this node.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/problems/process-conduct-is-unassured.flexiarg", :sha256 "11294171bd2e049cf21a741abe44bcd4a3e59d04c5cdf2670bdf2ddd5aa88ea2"}, :situation-source "Sentence s5 (offsets 244-325): the rule is attributed to `futon4/holes/mission-lifecycle.md`.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Until a checker refuses design content in HEAD, the rule is prose — but prose with a committed source pointer to the lifecycle document."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [8], :pattern "problems/process-conduct-is-unassured"} {:pattern-rationale "The constraint is declared up front so later content is triaged against it, not promoted early.", :fragment-span {:start 391, :end 404}, :occurrence-id ["inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end" 9], :roles ["condition"], :source-sha256 "8dde76d6103403d1561a5efec9e10736f7e3800201fb3058c278fd08f520a403", :sentence-id "s6", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end", :objects {:G {:text "    It is the only mechanism that attacks real uncommitted work at its source instead of sweeping it afterwards, and a sweep is an event that stops when its session dies.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end.flexiarg", :sha256 "8dde76d6103403d1561a5efec9e10736f7e3800201fb3058c278fd08f520a403"}, :situation-source "Fragment s6 (offsets 391-404): 'Nothing below' scopes the constraint to all subsequent content.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Promote the banner's own declared constraint over everything below, and hold the operator's raw sessions behind that gate."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    A turn ends having modified tracked or new files that are real work.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end.flexiarg", :sha256 "8dde76d6103403d1561a5efec9e10736f7e3800201fb3058c278fd08f520a403"}, :situation-source "Sentence s3 (offsets 117-141): '2026-09-28 (appended below, ...)' — real appended content sits below the banner.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "A turn of mission work ends having touched real, tracked content (the operator's appended sessions)."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Another seat may be editing the same files; the harness may have no turn-end hook; and a repo under continuous activity can stay \"in flight\" indefinitely, so an in-flight exemption can hide accumulation.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end.flexiarg", :sha256 "8dde76d6103403d1561a5efec9e10736f7e3800201fb3058c278fd08f520a403"}, :situation-source "Sentence s6 (offsets 341-364): 'carries tensions forward' — the material is deliberately held, not resolved.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The content below is the operator's, held in HEAD; promoting it early would resolve tensions another seat is still carrying."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Promote the turn's own attributed files behind gates, exempt other seats' live edits with recorded reasons, make holds loud, and report exemptions older than 24h as failures of the exemption, not as clean.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end.flexiarg", :sha256 "8dde76d6103403d1561a5efec9e10736f7e3800201fb3058c278fd08f520a403"}, :situation-source "Sentences s4-s7 (offsets 196-428): the constraints (not build, not design, no curriculum) are all declared before the appended material.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "Gating at the banner attacks misreading at its source: a reader who reaches the appended sessions has already passed the constraint that governs them."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [9], :pattern "inbox-zero/promote-at-turn-end"} {:pattern-rationale "The file refuses to over-advance into curriculum territory it has not reached.", :fragment-span {:start 405, :end 428}, :occurrence-id ["apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule" 10], :roles ["condition" "contrast"], :source-sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f", :sentence-id "s7", :blend-square {:schema :wm/three-halves-square-v1, :pattern "apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule", :objects {:G {:text "    Analysis capacity exists — the register's standard and the causal through-line were both produced by the same agents who spent weeks patching — but it activates only when the system is stopped; unscheduled, that happens exactly when the operator's patience breaks, which is the most expensive possible trigger.\n\n    + evidence: APM: 08-27 register standard unused for twelve days; 09-08 end-to-end analysis within hours of the forced halt. Convergent wm mechanism: self-halting loop that bells its owner; ruled walkthroughs as scheduled halts; steward drain contract.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Fragment s7 (offsets 405-428): 'specifies a curriculum.' — the refusal is pre-declared in the banner.", :theory {:elems #{:g}, :names {:g "Fix the scope boundary in the banner so no advance into curriculum territory needs anyone's courage to refuse."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I1 {:text "    Fixes keep landing but the same defect families keep recurring.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s7 (offsets 405-428): 'specifies a curriculum.' closes the banner by fixing scope.", :theory {:elems #{:i1}, :names {:i1 "The mission keeps recording operator sessions but its scope stays deliberately fixed."}, :axioms #{}}}, :I2 {:text "    Against a live campaign, every fix is minimal by necessity — nobody is ever authorized or situated to stop and rebuild a seam, because stopping always costs something visible today while the seam's cost is spread across future incidents.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentence s3 (offsets 117-141): the second session is 'appended below' to the standing banner.", :theory {:elems #{:i2}, :names {:i2 "The mission cannot stop the operator's sessions or rebuild the file into a curriculum; each session appends minimally."}, :axioms #{}}}, :B {:text "    Put the halt on the schedule so it needs no one's courage: between waves, stop cleanly, re-read the register, and convert \"guarantee: none\" rows into mechanisms — the register defines done as \"recurrence requires a named mechanism to fail\". Only then start the next wave. Register stewards drain between waves so no raw queue reaches the operator.\n", :source {:path "futon3/library/apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule.flexiarg", :sha256 "afb63a67df2f5323003c984b67b2db79795ba94d5f4528589892342ad28ef11f"}, :situation-source "Sentences s3-s4 (offsets 150-243): the sketch is requested '*as design*, not build' and the phase is 'Not yet IDENTIFY'.", :theory {:elems #{:b}, :names {:b "The design material (the operator's sketch request) exists in the file; it activates within scope when the lifecycle advances, not by expanding scope under pressure."}, :axioms #{}}}}, :maps {:a1 #{[:g :i1]}, :a2 #{[:g :i2]}, :b1 #{[:i1 :b]}, :b2 #{[:i2 :b]}}, :auxiliary {:b1 false, :b2 false}}, :fragment-indices [10], :pattern "apparatus/the-system-stops-on-schedule"}], :edges [{:from ["casc